6b. which one would you train in, and why
    fp32 error 1.49e-09 < bf16 error 9.77e-05 < fp8 error 1.56e-03
    bf16 keeps fp32's full 8-bit exponent range (same dynamic range, no loss-scaling knob)
    and pays for it in mantissa precision only — the §10 trade this session names as the
    reason bf16 replaced fp16. fp8 E4M3 is named here as the production recipe it now is,
    not as what this run trains in.

